    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0715" n="607" xml:id="pg607"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Blaine</hi>: I have just received a telegram
                    to the effect that Sir G. Baden-Powell leaves Liverpool this day by the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Etruria</hi> for New York, whence he will proceed to
                    Ottawa for a few days, and then come to Washington with Dr. Dawson. They hope to
                    be here on the 20th instant.</p>
                <p>Believe me, yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
